# Paths where a review is not optional.
#
# This file is INERT on its own. It has teeth only once the ruleset on `main`
# turns on "require review from Code Owners" — without that it is documentation.
# See the repository-settings commands in the pull-request review workflow.
#
# Two groups, for two different reasons.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRIVILEGED — runs outside any sandbox, on a maintainer's machine or in CI
# with real secrets. scripts/ and .githooks/ execute at commit time via
# core.hooksPath; .github/ decides what every other check is even allowed to
# do; package.json and bun.lock choose the code that `bun install` fetches.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/.github/          @queso
/.githooks/        @queso
/scripts/          @queso
/package.json      @queso
/bun.lock          @queso
/Dockerfile        @queso
/.dockerignore     @queso
/docker-compose*   @queso

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MODEL-FACING — becomes a prompt, a skill, or a flow definition. These are not
# executed, so no sandbox, allowlist or scanner has anything useful to say
# about them: the attack is text that redirects a model at run time, and in a
# diff it reads as ordinary prose. A human who knows what the prompt is FOR is
# the only control that works.
#
# triage/ is the sharpest: .github/workflows/triage.yml runs that flow against
# real issues with an `issues: write` token, from the `:main` image tag, which
# docker.yml rebuilds on every push to main. A merge here goes live with no
# further gate.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/triage/           @queso
/examples/         @queso
/fixtures/         @queso
*.flow.yaml        @queso
**/prompts/        @queso
**/SKILL.md        @queso

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NORMATIVE — SPEC.md states what the kernel must do, and CLAUDE.md is what
# steers every agent session. drift.lock records who last vouched for which
# prose; a diff that re-signs an anchor while changing no prose is the thing
# to look at.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/SPEC.md           @queso
/CLAUDE.md         @queso
/drift.lock        @queso
